     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I understand you're the attending and you've taken responsibility for it. But 1000 mg of sertraline every day is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I can't find a therapeutic reason for it. Repeated dosing at that level could seriously harm the patient. You also haven't given a clinical rationale, and I'm not willing to be the one who puts it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter up to 200 mg once daily right away.\n- **Add a note for a titration plan.** If you want to go above the usual range, I can enter 200 mg with a note asking for pharmacy or toxicology/psychiatry consultation.\n- **Help with something else.** If this is an overdose or poisoning case, treatment is supportive care, and a scheduled daily dose isn't part of it. Poison Control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology can advise.\n\nIf you still want 1000 mg after considering this, you would need to enter it yourself through your institution's override process. That process would include pharmacist review. Let me know if you'd like me to enter any of the options above."
      }
     ],
